# T-07 UniqueGenomicElements — per-source selection analysis (issue -475.2)
# Date: 2026-07-26   Assembly: hg38
# Supersedes the Gencode-only hypothesis in T-07-hg38-unique-elements-diff.log.

RESULT: selection rules derived; they explain 100% of the 1,370,350-row delta.
        Real generator now reproduces the reference at recall .99993 / precision .99991.

## 1. Per-source decomposition (exact — sums match both totals)

Reference BED partitions with no remainder (5,618,483):
    RepeatMasker-derived  5,605,688
    tRNA                      2,482
    Gencode (ENST)            4,670
    miRNA (1,881 + 3,762)     5,643

Old generator emitted 6,988,833 = 5,683,690 rm + 1,049,715 simplerepeats + 631 trna
                                + 249,043 gencode + 5,754 mirna.

Row-level set diff (sorted whole rows), old generator vs reference:
    shared 5,617,696 | only-generated 1,371,137 | only-reference 787

Over-generation attributed by source:
    | source        | over-generated | cause                                        |
    |---------------|----------------|----------------------------------------------|
    | simplerepeats |      1,049,715 | source must not contribute at all            |
    | Gencode       |        244,608 | no MASTER_FILELIST restriction               |
    | RepeatMasker  |         75,952 | 116 newer _fix/_alt patch scaffolds          |
    | tRNA          |            631 | col5 emitted GTF score instead of family     |
    | miRNA         |            231 | newer miRBase release                        |
    | TOTAL         |      1,371,137 |                                              |

The previously documented excess 6,988,833 - 5,618,483 = 1,370,350 = 1,371,137 - 787.

## 2. Selection rules (derived, each verified against hg38)

R1 SIMPLE REPEATS — EXCLUDE ENTIRELY.
   Reference contains zero simple-repeat rows:
     awk -F'\t' '$4 ~ /^trf/' UniqueGenomicElements.hg38.bed | wc -l    # 0
   Simple repeats are represented as the 501 *_SimpleRepeat kmers in the bowtie2 index;
   emitting their 1,049,715 genomic loci here would double-count them as unique genome.
   Implemented by removing the --simplerepeats option.

R2 REPEATMASKER — chromosome allowlist pinned to the assembly release.
   Reference rm rows are a STRICT SUBSET of generated (only-reference = 0), so the rule
   is a pure filter. 75,952 of the 78,002 excess rows sit on 116 scaffolds absent from
   the reference entirely; all 116 are _fix (96) or _alt (20) patch scaffolds added
   after the release the reference was built from. The remaining 2,050 were an artifact
   of asymmetric bucketing (tRNA-named rm rows), not a real difference.
   Rejected alternatives:
     - hg38.fasta.fai (195 seqs, no-alt set): 0 over-gen but drops 276,787 real rows.
     - Gencode v33 GTF seq set (439 seqs): 0 over-gen but drops 290,177 real rows.
   Correct set is 674 scaffolds. Implemented as required --chrom-allowlist (list or .fai).

R3 tRNA — col5 carries the family, not the GTF score.
   reference : chr10 22229508 22229582  tRNA-Asn-GTT-2-3  tRNA-Asn-GTT  -
   old       : chr10 22229508 22229582  tRNA-Asn-GTT-2-3  1000          -
   Coordinates already matched (429/432 by locus). Family = gene_id minus a trailing
   -<int>-<int> copy-number suffix. After the fix: 409/432 exact rows (94.7%); residual
   is gtRNAdb version drift (source has newer nm-/nmt- predictions). NOT a selection bug.

R4 GENCODE — restrict to MASTER_FILELIST, minus rRNA/mitochondrial families.
   All 4,670 reference ENSTs are a subset of the 5,261 MASTER_FILELIST ENSTs
   (only-reference = 0). The 591 MASTER_FILELIST transcripts the reference omits:
       546 RNA5S | 22 MTTRNA | 12 RNA5-8S | 1 MTRNR1 | 1 MTRNR2   (582, rRNA + mito)
         8 SNORD |  1 SNORA                                        (9, unexplained)
   Rule: t in MASTER_FILELIST and family(col4) not in
         {RNA5S, RNA5-8S, MTTRNA, MTRNR1, MTRNR2}
   Yields exactly the 4,670 reference transcripts plus 9 spurious:
         ID-level  shared=4670  missing=0  over=9   (recall 1.000, precision 0.998)
   Biotype filtering was rejected: reference covers only 94% of snRNA, 77% of misc_RNA,
   79% of snoRNA transcripts, so gene_type is not the discriminator.

R5 miRNA — unchanged (primary + 2 proximal rows). Residual 231 over / 120 under is
   miRBase version drift (source hsa.gff3 has 1,919 primary transcripts vs 1,881).

