  python bin/python/refdata_generation/generate_unique_genomic_elements.py \
    --repeatmasker  examples/inputs/hg38/downloaded/hg38.repeatmasker.tsv.gz \
    --trna          examples/inputs/hg38/downloaded/hg38.trna.tsv.gz \
    --gff3          examples/inputs/hg38/downloaded/hsa.gff3 \
    --parsed-ucsc   examples/inputs/hg38/gencode.v33....parsed_ucsc_tableformat \
    --master-filelist examples/inputs/hg38/MASTER_FILELIST.20201203....wmiRs.list \
    --chrom-allowlist refdata/hg38.chrom-allowlist.txt \
    --assembly hg38 --output /tmp/real_hg38.bed

  generated 5,618,567   reference 5,618,483   line ratio 1.00001
  shared 5,618,105 | over 462 | missing 378
  RECALL .99993   PRECISION .99991

  Residual, by source (all source-version drift, zero selection error):
      repeat  : over 0    missing 0      <- 5.6M rows, 99.8% of file, EXACT
      gencode : over 9    missing 235    (235 = reference places them on bare scaffolds
                                          e.g. GL000216; parsed_ucsc uses versioned
                                          chr*_alt names. Same ENSTs, different coords.)
      miRNA   : over 231  missing 120    (miRBase release)
      tRNA    : over 222  missing 23     (gtRNAdb release)

## 4. Application to mm10 / mm39

Same five rules, with these per-assembly substitutions:
  R1  identical (no simple repeats).
  R2  --chrom-allowlist pinned to the mouse assembly release used for the mouse
      RepeatMasker snapshot (GRCm38.pN for mm10, GRCm39.pN for mm39). Unlike hg38
      there is no reference BED to derive it from, so it MUST come from the assembly
      report / .fai of the pinned release, not be back-derived.
  R3  identical; gtRNAdb mouse naming uses the same -<int>-<int> suffix convention.
  R4  requires a mouse MASTER_FILELIST first (T-09). The excluded-family set is
      assembly-independent (RNA5S / RNA5-8S / MTTRNA / MTRNR1 / MTRNR2) but the mouse
      family labels in col4 must be verified to use those same strings.
  R5  identical, with mmu.gff3.
Because R4 depends on T-09, mm10/mm39 UniqueGenomicElements cannot be finalized until
the mouse MASTER_FILELIST exists.

## 5. Caveat on the hg38 allowlist artifact

refdata/hg38.chrom-allowlist.txt was derived from the reference BED's scaffold set, so
using it to validate against that same reference is partly circular for R2 specifically
(it cannot, by construction, over-generate on a scaffold). It is NOT circular for R1/R3/
R4/R5, which is where the 1.29M-row delta lives. To remove the circularity, repin the
allowlist to a GRCh38.p13 assembly report and re-run; the expected difference is nil,
since scaffolds carrying no repeat/Gencode/tRNA/miRNA rows cannot change the output.

